---
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'October 28, 2026';
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="Terms of Service — Framewrite"
  description="The terms that apply when you use Framewrite."
  path="/terms"
>
  <article class="legal">
    <div class="container legal-inner">
      <p class="legal-meta">Last updated {lastUpdated}</p>
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>

      <div class="legal-body">
        <p>
          These terms govern your use of <strong>Framewrite</strong> (framewrite.cc and
          app.framewrite.cc), including the web app and API. By creating an account or using the
          service, you agree to them. If you don't agree, please don't use Framewrite. Questions:
          <a href="mailto:contact@framewrite.cc">contact@framewrite.cc</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>The service</h2>
        <p>
          Framewrite turns video and audio into documents and transcripts, and offers related
          tools such as live transcription, document chat, and agents. Some of this runs in your
          browser; some of it sends your content to third-party providers, as described in our
          <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Your account</h2>
        <p>
          You sign in with Google. You're responsible for activity under your account and for
          keeping your API keys secret. You must be at least 13 years old, and old enough to form
          a binding contract where you live. Tell us if you think your account or a key has been
          compromised.
        </p>

        <h2>Your content</h2>
        <p>
          You keep ownership of the videos, audio, and other material you upload ("Your Content")
          and of the documents and transcripts generated from it. You give us a limited license
          to store, process, and transmit Your Content, including to our service providers, only
          as needed to operate the service for you.
        </p>
        <p>
          You promise that you have the rights needed to upload Your Content and to have it
          processed, including any consent required from people who appear or speak in it
          (recordings of other people can be subject to consent laws where you live). Generated
          output may be inaccurate or incomplete -- review it before relying on it.
        </p>

        <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>Don't use Framewrite to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>break the law or infringe anyone's intellectual property or privacy rights;</li>
          <li>upload content you don't have the right to process, or that is unlawful or abusive;</li>
          <li>probe, overload, or disrupt the service, or bypass usage limits or billing;</li>
          <li>reverse engineer the service or resell access to it without our written permission;</li>
          <li>share your account or API keys with others.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We may suspend or terminate access, and remove content, if we reasonably believe these
          terms are being violated.
        </p>

        <h2>Pricing and payment</h2>
        <p>
          Framewrite is pay-as-you-go: you top up a wallet through Stripe and are charged per
          unit of media processed, as shown on our pricing page at the time you submit a job.
          There are no subscriptions. If a job fails on our side, the charge for it is refunded
          to your wallet. Otherwise, wallet top-ups and completed jobs are non-refundable except
          where the law requires. We may change prices going forward; changes don't affect jobs
          already submitted.
        </p>

        <h2>Retention</h2>
        <p>
          Documents are kept for a limited time after processing (currently 7 days) and then
          deleted. Download anything you need before then. See the
          <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for details.
        </p>

        <h2>Google Drive</h2>
        <p>
          If you connect Google Drive, you authorize us to save documents you choose to your
          Drive. You can disconnect at any time from Settings, or revoke access at
          myaccount.google.com/permissions. Our use of information received from Google APIs
          follows the Google API Services User Data Policy, including its Limited Use
          requirements.
        </p>

        <h2>Our property</h2>
        <p>
          Framewrite, its software, branding, and design belong to us. These terms don't give you
          any rights to them beyond using the service as intended.
        </p>

        <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
        <p>
          We work to keep Framewrite running but don't promise uninterrupted or error-free
          service. We may change, add, or remove features. We may update these terms; if the
          change matters we'll update the date above, and continuing to use Framewrite afterward
          means you accept the update.
        </p>

        <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
        <p>
          Framewrite is provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties of any kind,
          express or implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and
          accuracy of generated output, to the fullest extent permitted by law.
        </p>

        <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the fullest extent permitted by law, Framewrite won't be liable for indirect,
          incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or for lost profits, data, or
          goodwill. Our total liability for any claim relating to the service is limited to the
          amount you paid us in the 12 months before the claim arose.
        </p>

        <h2>Termination</h2>
        <p>
          You can stop using Framewrite at any time, and can ask us to delete your account by
          emailing <a href="mailto:contact@framewrite.cc">contact@framewrite.cc</a>. We may
          suspend or end your access for violating these terms. Sections that by their nature
          should survive termination (ownership, disclaimers, liability limits) do.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          <a href="mailto:contact@framewrite.cc">contact@framewrite.cc</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</MarketingLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    padding: 56px 0 72px;
  }

  .legal-inner {
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .legal-meta {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: var(--step-4);
    margin: 0 0 32px;
    padding-bottom: 32px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .legal-body {
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .legal-body p,
  .legal-body ul {
    margin: 0 0 1.4em;
  }

  .legal-body ul {
    padding-left: 1.3em;
  }

  .legal-body li {
    margin-bottom: 0.6em;
  }

  .legal-body h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    margin: 1.6em 0 0.6em;
  }

  .legal-body a {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
</style>
